      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Sending out notifications to a ton of users is deceptively kinda difficult (Discord famously dealt with this for YEARS) but there's clever ways around it or to \"fake it\".\n\nDefinitely interested in doing so.\n\nOne challenge is that some platforms are really clunky to open URLs in. On Quest, platform restrictions prevent us from opening a browser without interrupting our own application (last I checked). On Android, you only get one tiny little screen. :(\n\nIs the idea here to promote the client update or SDK update notes, or to promote the ask forums? I'm on board for both, but one's harder than the other, because we can just buff up our efforts on the in-app article comms if we just want to promo the update notes.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
